1	line	Bolkoy	Hello there. You're that hero who saved the orbs. Soon we will perform the ritual and the village will be safe again.
1	line	Bolkoy	Anyway, would you like anything from my shop?
1	option	What have you got?
1	option	No thank you.
0	section	Talking to King Bolren without the orbs after getting them
1	line	Player	Bolren, I have returned.
1	line	King Bolren	You made it back! Do you have the orbs?
1	line	Player	No, I'm afraid not.
1	line	King Bolren	Please, we must have the orbs if we are to survive.
1	action	end
0	section	Return of the orb
1	line	Player	Bolren, I have returned.
1	line	King Bolren	You made it back! Do you have the orbs?
1	line	Player	I have them here.
1	line	King Bolren	Hooray, you're amazing. I didn't think it was possible but you've saved us.
1	line	King Bolren	Once the orbs are replaced we will be safe once more. We must begin the ceremony immediately.
1	line	Player	What does the ceremony involve?
1	line	King Bolren	The spirit tree has looked over us for centuries. Now we must pay our respects.
1	box	The gnomes begin to chant. Meanwhile, King Bolren holds the orbs of protection out in front of him.
1	line	[Northern Local Gnomes]	Su tana.
1	line	[Southern Local Gnomes]	En tania.
1	line	[Northern Local Gnomes]	Su tana.
1	line	[Southern Local Gnomes]	En tania.
1	box	The orbs of protection come to rest gently in the branches of the ancient spirit tree.
1	line	King Bolren	Now at last my people are safe once more. We can live in peace again.
1	line	Player	I'm pleased I could help.
1	line	King Bolren	You are modest brave traveller.
1	line	King Bolren	Please, for your efforts take this amulet. It's made from the same sacred stone as the orbs of protection. It will help keep you safe on your journeys.
1	line	Player	Thank you King Bolren.
1	line	King Bolren	The tree has many other powers, some of which I cannot reveal. As a friend of the gnome people, I can now allow you to use the tree's magic to teleport to other trees grown from related seeds.
